{
  "name": "positional-member-fixability",
  "description": "Deleting a constant of a block can change a constant after it: a later specification repeats its expression list, a later expression list uses iota, or removing one name of a specification leaves fewer names than the list a later specification repeats. The enum-group class retains such a constant whenever a constant it changes is one code names, or where removing it alone does not compile, so it is never reported, and a declaration only it names stays live with it. A wholly dead group whose specifications declare several names and repeat a list is retained too, because no name of it can be removed alone. A dead constant whose deletion changes no named constant is reported with its code's own fixability, and shares a component with each dead constant whose value its deletion changes. A specification that writes no expression list references the type the repeated list names, so an enumerated type a live member repeats stays live.",
  "languages": ["go"],
  "target_kind": "application",
